    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d202">

                <pb facs="0263" n="171" sameAs="frus:frus1943CairoTehran/pg171"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 Moscow/256a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stettinius</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Ambassador in
                        the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Harriman</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">u. s. urgent</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-11-09">November 9, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1180. Secret and personal for the Ambassador from the Acting Secretary.</p>
                <p>The President has handed to me your message no. 6100 sent via Navy.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d202-f1"/> You are authorized to comply with Molotov’s request that your letter containing
                    the message concerning Turkey be made a part of the secret military record of
                    the Conference.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Stettinius</hi></signed><lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Acting</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d202-f1" n="1" xml:id="d202-f1-content">
                <p>This is the telegram of November 6, <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref
                        target="#pg158">p. 158</ref>.</p>
